diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index d532f62..7d6ae44 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -3,18 +3,21 @@
 A small command-line task tracker that stores tasks in a JSON file.
 
 ```
-tasker add [-p N] <title words...>     add a task (priority 1-5, default 3)
-tasker list [--all] [--sort id|priority] list open tasks (or all)
+tasker add [-p N] [--tag T] [--due YYYY-MM-DD] <title words...>  add a task (priority 1-5, default 3; --tag is repeatable)
+tasker list [--all] [--sort id|priority|due] [--tag T] [--overdue]  list open tasks (or all; --tag is repeatable)
 tasker done <id>                        mark a task done
 tasker rm <id>                          delete a task
-tasker edit <id> [-p N] [--title T]     change priority or title
+tasker edit <id> [-p N] [--title T] [--tag T] [--untag T] [--due YYYY-MM-DD|none]  change priority, title, tags or due date
+tasker tags                             print each tag used by open tasks with its count
 ```
 
+Tasks may carry tags (lower-cased `a-z0-9` words with hyphens, e.g. `home`, `tax-2026`) and an optional due date. `list --overdue` shows not-done tasks whose due date is strictly before today, and `list --sort due` orders by due date with undated tasks last.
+
 The data file is `$TASKER_FILE` (default `tasks.json` in the current directory).
 
 ## Layout
 - `internal/model` — the Task type and validation.
-- `internal/store` — loading/saving the JSON file (with a schema `version`).
+- `internal/store` — loading/saving the JSON file (with a schema `version`; files are saved as version 2, version-1 files still load).
 - `internal/query` — filtering and sorting.
 - `internal/cli` — argument parsing, commands and output formatting. `cli.Run` is the testable entry point.
 - `cmd/tasker` — main.
